From 29144aaf894a27017e52a22ffb42f3a646087e8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:13:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0269 -- retire the AUDIOPRB audio-cost timings
 (SDL side)

Removes the S7 / S7-GUS "TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC" timers and their snapshot accessors:
SDL_DOSOpl3WriteRegister's per-call timing (0141), SDL_DOSGusGetState's (0145), the five
GUS voice calls' (0146), the GUS PIO upload and UploadSample brackets (0147), and 0199's
SDL_DOSAudioDiagTiming() switch (SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_DIAG_TIMING) with its SDL_dos.h /
SDL_dos_audio_synth.h declarations. SDL_DOSOpl3WriteRegister -- on the OPL hot path, also
replayed from the SB ISR -- loses its per-write hint test.

Off by default since 0199; the only consumer was dosags ags's AUDIOPRB dump, retired by
ags 0352 in the same step; the investigation (the GUS 6.89 s slot-poll outlier) concluded.
The separate GUS_DIAG ring (g_gus_diag, gus_diag_put/flush, SDL/0112) is a different
diagnostic and stays. Local to this port's patches/SDL; no hub change.
---
